Article 8 (Infrastructure Development Division)
(1) The Head of the Infrastructure Development Division shall be a public official of Grade IV.
(2) The Head of the Infrastructure Development Division shall be responsible for the following matters:
1. Approval of plans for developing infrastructure for the management of high-level radioactive waste;
2. Matters concerning research and development for managing high-level radioactive waste;
3. Site selection, construction, and operation of underground research facilities within sites for high-level radioactive waste disposal facilities;
4. Site selection, construction, and operation of underground research facilities for research purposes;
5. Implementation of projects to train technical professionals in the management of high-level radioactive waste;
6. Designation of and cancellation of designation of institutions for training technical professionals in the management of high-level radioactive waste;
7. Establishment and management of cooperation systems among industry, academia, and research institutions relating to the management of high-level radioactive waste;
8. International cooperation relating to high-level radioactive waste management affairs.
